    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "previous sanctions on Iran after France, Germany, \nand the UK triggered the snapback mechanism,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "determining that Iran had been violating \nits nuclear commitments for years and had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accumulated a stockpile of highlyenriched uranium \nthat lacked any credible civilian justification.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the sanctions environment right now is \nactually at its most restrictive in years. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the snapback mechanism was specifically designed \nso that no single country can veto it, including  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "America. If any participant in the original deal \ntriggers it, sanctions return automatically within  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587200,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "30 days. There is no appeals process. There is no \nnegotiation. They just come back. On top of that,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iran's entire banking system is effectively \ncut off from the global financial network.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The major Iranian banks are sanctioned, which \nmeans moving money in and out of the country  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through normal channels is uh complicated and \nany private company that gets it wrong faces  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "secondary sanctions from the US Treasury. In a \nchoice between doing some business with Iran and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doing some business with the USA, the largest \ncapital and consumer market in the world,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iran is generally not going to be seen as \nworthwhile. The idea that a non-binding memorandum  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619920,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of understanding is going to provide enough legal \nclarity for private companies to commit hundreds  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624160,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of billions of dollars into this environment is uh \noptimistic. Oh, and by the way, Iran's access to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this fund is supposed to be conditional on Tyrron \ndismantling its nuclear program, eliminating its  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stockpiles of enriched uranium, and accepting a \nstringent inspection regime. So, as an investor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if you were comfortable with all of the other \nrisks, you would also be betting that the Iranian  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "government is going to voluntarily give up its \nnuclear program, which has historically not been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a winning bet. They agreed to limit enrichment \nunder the JCPOA and then blew past those limits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the moment it became convenient. By mid 2025, the \nInternational Atomic Energy Commission confirmed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661840,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iran had accumulated enough enriched uranium for \nmultiple nuclear weapons. Okay. Okay. But let's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say all of that somehow works out and the deal \nsticks. You are also now investing into a country  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673120,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that has a pretty well doumented history of just \ntaking stuff. Following the 1979 revolution,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the new government nationalized nearly \nevery major industry in the country. Banks,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insurance companies, steel, copper, aluminum, \nmining, automobile manufacturing. All of it was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688640,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seized on July 5th of that year. Foreign joint \nventures were voided overnight. Contracts with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decades left to run were simply declared invalid \nby the revolutionary courts. And if Iran decides  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do it again, what exactly are investors \ngoing to do? We've already tried using force,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's kind of how we got into this whole mess \nin the first place. Huh. Now, even setting aside  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the political risk in this riskreward analysis, \nit's also worth pointing out that the reward  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715200,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't exactly that great either. Iran's economy \nis not exactly uh what you'd call a particularly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attractive investment market right now. According \nto the IMF, Iran's GDP is expected to contract by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726800,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "6.1% this year, and inflation is projected to \nhit 68.9% with food prices already running 99%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733600,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher year-over-year as of February. The real has \ndepreciated by 44% year-over-year and was already  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740320,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at record lows before the war even started, \ntrading at 1,750,000 to1 US as of late 2025.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its oil infrastructure has been deteriorating \nfor years, declining reservoir productivity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aging equipment being cannibalized for parts, and \nvirtually no investment in enhanced recovery. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this was all before a war further damaged it. \nEven if that infrastructure is fully rebuilt,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are still limits in place on who Iran can \nsell this oil to. According to Iran International,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "86% of the tankers transporting Iranian oil over \nthe past year have themselves been sanctioned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the United States. And Iranian crude is \ncurrently priced about $11 to $12 per barrel  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "below comparable benchmarks, significantly \ncutting into Tyrron's net revenue. Even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781920,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside of fossil fuels, the local market is \ndominated by government-controlled businesses,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limiting opportunities to generate returns inside \nthe domestic economy. Allowing investors to put  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790960,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "money into Iran is kind of like the government \ngiving investors the green light to invest in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Logan Paul's latest crypto project. I mean, \nit's technically nice that you're allowed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but history would suggest it's probably not a \ngood idea. Now, I realize that might sound like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm being overly harsh, and look, every emerging \nmarket comes with risk. That's literally why the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "returns are supposed to be higher. Investors \ntake calculated bets on unstable countries all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the time. But the difference here is that \nin a normal emerging market investment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have some kind of legal framework to protect \nyour capital. Bilateral investment treaties,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world bank arbitration, or international courts. \nIn Iran, under the current sanctions regime,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most of those protections either don't apply \nor can't be enforced. You'd be investing with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentially zero legal recourse if something \ngoes wrong. And it's not like reconstruction  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investments have a great track record to begin \nwith, even when the US has far more control over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how the money is spent. In Iraq, the US put \nover $60 billion into reconstruction grants.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The special inspector general found that at least \n$8 billion was outright wasted and another 10% of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the total couldn't be accounted for at all. The \nwhole thing resulted in 87 fraud indictments. In  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856000,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Afghanistan, it was worse. $144 billion spent over \n20 years with somewhere between 26 and $29 billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasted on ghost schools, ghost teachers, ghost \npolice forces, and buildings that collapsed almost  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "immediately after they were built. And those were \ncountries where the US had boots on the ground.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An inspector general's office running constant \naudits and at least some degree of political  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alignment with the reconstruction goals. In \nIran, you would have none of that. private  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capital going into a country with no friendly \nmilitary presence, no oversight infrastructure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a hostile government, and a legal system that \nhas historically treated foreign assets as, to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889760,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "put it generously, negotiable. And remember, those \nwere also situations where the US government was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spending its own money with inspectors reporting \nto Congress. This deal is asking private companies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to take that risk with shareholders money and \neven less oversight. But okay, fine, fine, fine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fine. Let's play devil's advocate. Anyway, the \none piece of good news is that the structure to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910880,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do these deals is kind of already in place. Say \nyou wanted to invest $100 million into Iran. What  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would typically do is commit that money to \nan offshore specialurpose vehicle or SPV that you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "control in a neutral jurisdiction. Typically, \nan accommodating financial city like Dubai,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926800,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hong Kong, or Geneva. That SPV then spends the \n$100 million offshore, paying equipment makers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and engineering contractors directly to rebuild \na specific revenue generating asset in Iran,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937760,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say a refinery unit or part of the Mabaraka steel \ncomplex. Iran receives the finished asset, not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a dollar of cash. Once it's running, Iran repays \nin kind. It ships an agreed volume of crude over,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949120,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say, 3 years. That oil is sold most likely to a \nChinese or Indian refiner who pays market price  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955520,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly 130 million over the term. But instead \nof paying it to Iran, they pay it back to your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SPV. In this system, money never actually goes \nto Iran or gets caught up in their sanctioned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966320,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "banking system. Stuff goes into Iran and oil comes \nout. No money. Now on paper, that structure looks  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973040,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clean enough. And it is basically how Chinese, \nRussian, and Indian firms already operate in Iran.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chinese investment through structures like these \nhas exceeded $15 billion over the last decade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although exact figures are hard to pin down \nbecause neither side is keen on publishing them.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a great system to avoid handing a blank check \nto a hostile regime. The problem is they can still  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just take the stuff. This structure really only \nworks these days because most of these agreements  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are made between Russian, Chinese or Indian firms. \nSo if Iran tries to screw over these businesses,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would be isolating themselves from one of \nthe few friends they have left. If Iran seized US  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assets or assets from western or western aligned \nstates, they weren't friendly to begin with. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012640,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unless these countries are willing to go back \nto war again, what can they do? It sounds bad,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it gets worse. There is one more inconvenient \ndetail that makes this structure particularly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fragile for new investors. And that is simply \nnobody has even figured out who is running the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028720,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fund yet. When asked how the reconstruction and \ndevelopment fund would actually be administered,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the people negotiating this deal essentially \nsaid, \"We'll figure that out later.\" As of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time of making this video, there is currently no \noversight board, no dispute resolution mechanism,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and no independent auditor. Okay, so with all \nof this in mind, who the is actually going to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "put their money into this? Realistically, probably \nnobody. It's basically gambling unless the returns  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are astronomical. Without any kind of government \nguarantee, the riskreward just isn't worth it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No sane fiduciary is putting a pension fund or \nendowment into this. And any CEO who committed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064080,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shareholder capital to Iran right now would have \na very interesting conversation with their board  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the moment the deal wobbles. The compliance costs \nalone would be staggering. You'd need an army of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sanctions lawyers fak advisers and political \nrisk consultants just to get started. This is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to say nothing of the optics and potential brand \ndamage of gaining involved in a regime that is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still massively unpopular around the world. At the \nmoment, the only source was published by Reuters,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088480,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relying on the word of one unnamed individual who \nsaid that over half of the money had already been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "committed by companies in South Korea, Singapore, \nMalaysia, Japan, and America itself. That is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099360,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flimsy at best. Over half of $300 billion means at \nleast $150 billion in private capital supposedly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "committed to one of the most hostile business \nenvironments on Earth. based on the word of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one person that Reuters won't name for a fund that \ndoesn't have an administrator, a legal structure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115920,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or final agreement behind it. For context, the \nentire global private equity industry raised  "
